**Definition 155.1 (All 190 indexed rows).** Order words lexicographically
with $0<1$. For each word other than $1^6$, list in order the events
$\{0\}$, $\{n(b)\}$, $\{0,n(b)\}$. The last word has only $\{0\}$.
Number rows $j=0,\ldots,189$. Write its word and event as $b_j,E_j$,
and write its lower bound as

$$
d_j(x)=k_j+\sum_{i=1}^6t_{ji}a_i-e.
\tag{155.1}
$$

For first zero $n$, the three pairs $(k_j,t_j)$ are
$(1,-e_n^{\rm in})$, $(0,e_n^{\rm in})$, $(1,0)$; at $1^6$ use $(1,0)$.
Thus the definitions determine every row, including all multiple-zero
words. The following compact word table specifies all row addresses.
The entry $j_0$ is the first row of that word; its three rows are
$j_0,j_0+1,j_0+2$, except for the final one-row word.

